WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:05.309
Open the battery-charger sample: a complete drawing set, 23 pages.

2
00:00:05.559 --> 00:00:18.208
Cover, contents, single-line, multi-line power, PLC, terminals, wire list, BOM.

3
00:00:18.458 --> 00:00:27.664
Place a contactor coil from the library: its designation is assigned by itself.

4
00:00:27.914 --> 00:00:40.805
Place its contact: same device, and the cross-references appear on both.

5
00:00:41.055 --> 00:00:46.132
Give the device a part from the library: the BOM will know about it.

6
00:00:46.382 --> 00:00:58.252
Number the wires with your own pattern: 020L+, 021L+ ...

7
00:00:58.502 --> 00:01:09.432
Conductors in their IEC 60757 colours; a bundle gets a single label.

8
00:01:09.682 --> 00:01:14.486
Reports come from the schematic. The terminal diagram ...

9
00:01:14.736 --> 00:01:17.884
... the wire list with the new numbers ...

10
00:01:18.134 --> 00:01:24.186
... and the BOM, which already counts the new contactor.

11
00:01:24.436 --> 00:01:31.145
Print preview: the page exactly as it prints.

12
00:01:31.395 --> 00:01:34.865
Export the PDF drawing set ...

13
00:01:35.115 --> 00:01:40.864
... and every list as one XLSX workbook.

14
00:01:41.114 --> 00:01:45.624
CablePilot: free, open source, your files stay yours.
